# OpenEVV sound map: Vietnamese (Northern) (eSpeak NG voice aav/vi), spoken by openevv's German module
# with the sounds, the melody and the tones of the language itself.
# Written by engine/accent/mapwriter.py; OpenEvvFrontend reads it, and docs/LANGUAGES.md
# says what each line means. Edit freely: the file is read each time a voice starts.

template dedx
style standard
vowels i I e E a A u U o O y Y oe OE @ aj aw oj a~ E~ o~ oe~ E: R
glides j w
schwa @
secondary 2
words apart
onset 1
cluster k w

# the melody: tone; a question that wants yes or no: rise
accent f0=own range=120 level=30 decl=6 declmax=25 lag=70 lead=15 fs=-6 fq=6 qreg=18 fc=4 fe=0 fw=-4 span=1 stressed=88 weak=112 stop=1

# the tones, under eSpeak NG's names for them
tone 1 p=0:33,100:32
tone 7 p=0:33,100:26
tone 2 p=0:22,100:11 brth=20
tone 3 p=0:32,35:32,100:50
tone 4 p=0:30,50:11,100:30 creak=25 cfrom=35 cto=65 dur=110
tone 5 p=0:32,40:26,60:30,100:52 creak=70 cfrom=35 cto=60
tone 6 p=0:30,100:12 dur=65 creak=60 cfrom=50 cto=100 stop=35

# what the module says in place of a phone it is given
says C t S
says J d Z
says P p f
says T t s

# the sounds of the language that the module has not, each as it differs from the phone
# that stands for it: formants and lengths in per cent, times in milliseconds
# realization master (engine/packs/master.py): each sound from the IPA master table (ipa/table) through the
# adapter, as it differs from the template's phone; its comment names the table entries and the provenance of their values
